NAME
    wc - count lines, words and bytes

SYNOPSIS
    wc [file | glob | -] ...

DESCRIPTION
    Prints three counts, "lines words bytes", for the files named taken
    together as one stream (globs expand, "-" is the console), or for
    the console up to Ctrl-D. A line is an LF; a word is a run of
    anything but space, tab, CR and LF. The counts are 32-bit (see
    num). wc is /BIN/WC.

LIMITS
    Up to 24 names in all, after glob expansion.

EXAMPLES
    wc /FRUIT.TXT                7 21 98
    wc /FRUIT.TXT /FRUIT2.TXT    14 42 192 (one line of totals)
    wc                           typed text, counted at Ctrl-D

NOTES
    One line of totals, never a line per file.
    Removed from the P8X version: input from a pipe or a < redirect.
    Changed: 32-bit counts (were 24-bit), several files and "-".
    Ported from P8X os/commands/wc.c 2026-09-23.

SEE ALSO
    cat, grep, sort, num, stdin
